        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211-a1">

                <pb facs="0284" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg202"/>

                <head>Mr. Campbell to Count
                        Manderstrom</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Stockholm,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 8, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to call the attention of
                    his Majesty’s government to several proclamations issued by the President of the
                    United States of America, dated, respectively, on the 11th ultimo, and each
                    herewith enclosed, in print, and attested by the undersigned.</p>
                <p>The first (enclosure No. 1) relates to the closing of certain ports of entry of
                    the United States; the second (enclosure No. 2) relates to the port of Key West,
                    in Florida; and the third (enclosure No. 3) has reference to the exchange of
                    reciprocal hospitalities between war vessels of the United States of America and
                    similar vessels of foreign powers in the ports of their respective
                    countries.</p>
                <p>In the language of the proclamation last referred to, (enclosure No. 3,) it is
                    believed by the President that, “whatever claim or pretence may have existed
                    heretofore, the United States are now, at least, entitled to claim and concede
                    an entire and friendly equality of rights and hospitalities with all maritime
                    nations.”</p>
                <p>In requesting the attention of his Majesty’s government to the proclamations
                    enclosed, I seize the occasion to assure you, sir, of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES H. CAMPBELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Count Manderstrom,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of State and of Foreign Affairs, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
